WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.062
00–zero:twenty — Hook

2
00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:06.841
nineteen thirty-nine.

3
00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:10.486
Europe stood on the edge of catastrophe.

4
00:00:10.986 --> 00:00:12.906
Within months,

5
00:00:13.406 --> 00:00:18.373
a conflict that began in Europe would expand across continents and oceans,

6
00:00:18.974 --> 00:00:25.358
drawing dozens of nations and hundreds of millions of people into the deadliest war in human history.

7
00:00:26.007 --> 00:00:29.751
twenty–zero:fifty — The Beginning

8
00:00:30.251 --> 00:00:35.892
On September 1st, nineteen thirty-nine, Nazi Germany invaded Poland.

9
00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:40.859
Britain and France responded by declaring war on Germany.

10
00:00:41.509 --> 00:00:51.037
What followed was a rapid German offensive across Europe, using coordinated tanks, aircraft, and infantry in a strategy that became known as Blitzkrieg.

11
00:00:51.537 --> 00:00:55.353
fifty–one:twenty — Europe Falls

12
00:00:55.853 --> 00:01:00.893
By nineteen forty, German forces had occupied much of Western Europe.

13
00:01:01.493 --> 00:01:06.030
France fell, while Britain resisted through the Battle of Britain.

14
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:12.176
In the skies above Britain, the Royal Air Force fought to prevent a German invasion.

15
00:01:12.775 --> 00:01:16.304
But the war was about to become even larger.

16
00:01:17.054 --> 00:01:21.614
twenty–one:fifty — The War Becomes Global

17
00:01:22.263 --> 00:01:30.855
In June nineteen forty-one, Germany launched Operation Barbarossa, invading the Soviet Union and opening the massive Eastern Front.

18
00:01:31.355 --> 00:01:37.164
Then, on December 7th, nineteen forty-one, Japan attacked Pearl Harbor.

19
00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:43.884
The United States entered the war, transforming the conflict into a truly global struggle.

20
00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:53.754
From North Africa to the Pacific, from the Atlantic Ocean to the Eastern Front, enormous armies and fleets were now engaged in battle.

21
00:01:54.403 --> 00:01:58.028
fifty–two:twenty — Turning Point

22
00:01:58.528 --> 00:02:02.343
The Axis powers initially appeared unstoppable.

23
00:02:02.843 --> 00:02:08.532
But during nineteen forty-two and nineteen forty-three, the momentum began to change.

24
00:02:09.132 --> 00:02:13.860
The Battle of Midway weakened Japanese naval power in the Pacific.

25
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:19.334
In North Africa, Allied forces pushed back Axis armies.

26
00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:25.497
And at Stalingrad, Soviet forces surrounded and defeated a major German army.

27
00:02:26.098 --> 00:02:29.265
The tide of the war had begun to turn.

28
00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:35.704
twenty–two:45 — D-Day and the Collapse of Nazi Germany

29
00:02:36.354 --> 00:02:43.602
On June 6th, nineteen forty-four, Allied forces launched D-Day, landing on the beaches of Normandy.

30
00:02:44.102 --> 00:02:47.701
The invasion opened a new front in Western Europe.

31
00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:53.506
Allied armies pushed toward Germany while Soviet forces advanced from the east.

32
00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:58.349
In May nineteen forty-five, Nazi Germany surrendered.

33
00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:03.913
45–three:00 — The Pacific and the Legacy

34
00:03:04.514 --> 00:03:13.105
The war continued against Japan until August nineteen forty-five, when atomic bombs were dropped on Hiroshima and Nagasaki.

35
00:03:13.756 --> 00:03:16.756
Japan surrendered shortly afterward.

36
00:03:17.355 --> 00:03:19.948
World War II had ended.

37
00:03:20.598 --> 00:03:23.765
More than sixty million people had died.

38
00:03:24.265 --> 00:03:29.906
Nations had been destroyed, borders redrawn, and a new global order emerged.

39
00:03:30.506 --> 00:03:36.169
The war was over—but its consequences would shape the world for generations.

40
00:03:36.819 --> 00:03:38.692
End screen:

41
00:03:39.292 --> 00:03:44.187
World War II — nineteen thirty-nine–nineteen forty-five

42
00:03:44.937 --> 00:03:48.153
The war that changed the modern world.
